PARITY NOTES
  • Unit conversion at the display boundary only (ADR-009 / Phase-48): outside_temp °C via
    convertTempFromSI (°C identity, °F = c*9/5+32); efficiency Wh/km → Wh/mi via the inline
    KM_PER_MILE factor exactly as the web source (no SI-energy helper exists). SI never stored/computed
    in non-SI. Numbers via fmtNumber-parity (default precision 2). Verified by Tests.
  • Temperature-bucket colors map 1:1 to design tokens whose hues EQUAL the web hex
    (chartSeriesSpeed=#3b82f6, chartSeriesRegen=#06b6d4, chartSeriesBattery=#10b981,
    chartSeriesEnergy=#f59e0b, chartSeriesTemperature=#ef4444) — token-compliant AND web-exact.
  • All 8 panels render in BOTH the success and empty phases (web "always show with placeholder"
    parity); loading shows the skeleton, error shows a retry. ADR-013 freshness chip + stale/offline
    banner + one-shot stale auto-refresh implemented and unit-tested.
  • Strings: 22 parity keys carry the verbatim web key names + English defaults in the platform
    string catalog; 6 page-scoped ADR-013/retry keys + the shared chart.noData added likewise. Zero
    hardcoded user-facing literals in the views.

